{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"aa870cd0534b1d1fb899c72be85669782d6e44e36f36b5c13ea39966317e95db","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler idempotency integration test","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py:311","binding_store_mod._now_iso","binding_lifecycle._now_iso","binding_lifecycle.clear_absent","binding_lifecycle.py:45","binding_lifecycle.py:296","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence"],"problem_keywords":["idempotency","test oracle","clock patching","integration test","module relocation","timestamp stamping","no-churn contract"],"propositions":["The idempotency oracle patches _now_iso on binding_store but RP-02 S2 T2 moved absence/tombstone operations (clear_absent, siblings) to binding_lifecycle which resolves its own _now_iso, causing the freeze to no longer reach the moved operations.","The integration test's blast radius narrowed after the module relocation: it would not catch a regression where clear_absent stamps updated_at unconditionally on an unchanged reconcile pass.","The unit-tier test test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence already pins the no-stamp contract directly on the policy owner, containing the coverage risk.","Patching _now_iso on both binding_store and binding_lifecycle restores the integration oracle's original reach and detection capability for timestamp stamping regressions."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787312199782754001,"uuid":"9b4bb2a8-2b3e-4415-92bc-4fd099382a40"}